{#
  The header of a folded box of « Le dossier »: its name, its telling
  figure, a chevron.

  Embedded rather than included, because the figure differs for every box
  and is the one thing that has to be refreshable — the caller supplies it
  in the `figure` block, wrapped in its own `data-booking-panel`:

    {% embed '@rental/management/_dossier_header.html.twig' with {
        box: boxes.payment, target_id: 'box-payment',
    } only %}
        {% block figure %}<span data-booking-panel="payment-figure">…</span>{% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}

  Same composition as Configuration > Maintenance's `section_header`, and
  for the same reason: `.btn` fixes its own colour AND its own font-size, so
  an `h6` put on the heading itself would deliver neither — the size goes on
  the span inside.

  Boxes ship folded. `box` is a Booking\BookingBox, which is also what the
  journey's links are built from, so the card id a link aims at and the
  panel this button opens can never be two different strings.

  Requires `box` and `target_id`.
#}
<h3 class="mb-0">
    <button type="button"
            class="btn collapsed w-100 d-flex align-items-center gap-2 p-3 text-start"
            data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#{{ target_id }}"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="{{ target_id }}">
        <span class="h6 mb-0 flex-grow-1">{{ box.label }}</span>
        {% block figure %}{% endblock %}
        <i class="bi bi-chevron-down text-body-tertiary" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>
</h3>
